<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piero di Lorenzo de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1472–1503</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Piero the Unfortunate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piero di <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo de' Medici</a> (1472–1503), known as Piero the Unfortunate, was the eldest son of Lorenzo de' Medici and ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> from 1492 to 1494. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france">Charles VIII of France</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1494, he surrendered key fortresses without the city's consent and was expelled with his family. He died in exile, drowned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garigliano">Garigliano river</a> while serving with the French army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piero-di-lorenzo-de-medici.jpg" alt="Piero di Lorenzo de' Medici" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gherardo di Giovanni del Fora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piero_di_Lorenzo_de_Medici_-_Domenico_Ghirlandaio.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
